Index: doc/Encoding.3
==================================================================
--- doc/Encoding.3
+++ doc/Encoding.3
@@ -381,10 +381,19 @@
 .CE
 .PP
 This \fIfreeProc\fR function is called when the encoding is deleted.  The
 \fIclientData\fR parameter is the same as the \fIclientData\fR field
 specified to \fBTcl_CreateEncoding\fR when the encoding was created.
+.PP
+\fIFreeProc\fR is called while Tcl holds its internal encoding lock, which
+is not reentrant.  It therefore must not call any function that takes this
+lock, such as \fBTcl_GetEncoding\fR, \fBTcl_GetEncodingFromObj\fR,
+\fBTcl_FreeEncoding\fR, \fBTcl_GetEncodingNames\fR,
+\fBTcl_CreateEncoding\fR or \fBTcl_SetSystemEncoding\fR (directly or
+through other Tcl functions, such as \fBTcl_EvalObjEx\fR); doing so
+deadlocks.  Nor should it wait for another thread that may be calling one of
+these functions.
 .PP
 \fBTcl_GetEncodingSearchPath\fR and \fBTcl_SetEncodingSearchPath\fR
 are called to access and set the list of filesystem directories searched
 for encoding data files.
 .PP

